    answer: '- Turn on tolerant parsing (`ignoreUnknownKeys`) and give enums/sealed discriminators a fallback branch — unknown values must never crash an old client\n- Field additions are safe; renames, type changes, removals are breaking: deprecation windows, version headers, tolerant client ships first\n- Enforce the contract with generated models and CI schema-compat tests, and alert on deserialization errors like crashes'
